SCOPE OF THIS NOTICE
====================

This MIT notice covers the vendored `mattpocock/skills` set ONLY -- the 23 skill
directories claimed by docs/agents/mattpocock-skills-manifest.json. It is the
shared notice for that one provider, which is why those 23 directories carry no
licence file of their own. It does NOT license this directory as a whole.

.claude/skills/ holds 81 vendored skills from six providers under three
different licences (MIT, Apache-2.0 and CC BY-SA 4.0). Every skill directory
outside the mattpocock set carries its own licence file; read that file, not
this one:

  Provider                                   Skills  Licence          Notice
  -----------------------------------------  ------  ---------------  ----------------------
  mattpocock/skills                              23  MIT              this file (shared)
  anthropics/skills                               3  Apache-2.0       <skill>/LICENSE.txt
  EveryInc/compound-engineering-plugin           22  MIT              <skill>/LICENSE
  trailofbits/skills                             23  CC BY-SA 4.0     <skill>/LICENSE
  github/awesome-copilot                          5  MIT              <skill>/LICENSE
  BuilderIO/skills                                5  MIT              <skill>/LICENSE

Note in particular that the 23 trailofbits/skills directories are CC BY-SA 4.0,
a copyleft licence with ShareAlike and modification-marking obligations that MIT
does not impose. Do not assume MIT terms for anything outside the mattpocock set.

Which provider owns a given skill directory is recorded in
docs/agents/<provider>-skills-manifest.json, and enforced by
scripts/validate-agent-governance.py. This repository's own source code is
GPL-3.0 and is licensed separately from all of the above.

The unmodified mattpocock/skills MIT notice follows.

